# An xor of thread index fields reads as one variable, the xor of its
# runs of thread bits; added to the shared base it is the store's
# address, 4 wavefronts per warp request, ideal 1
# (micro/xor_swizzle.ptx, whose stored offsets an RTX 4090 reads back as
# its header gives). One side of micro_xor_overlap's xor is a sum whose
# fields share a bit, which is no xor of them, and stays unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/xor_swizzle.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.shared.u32 	[%r8+64], %r1; // shared store [(16·(⌊%tid.x/8⌋ mod 4) ⊕ 16·(%tid.x mod 128)) + buf + 64] wavefronts/req 4 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.shared.u32 	[%r9], %r1; // shared store addr ? (depends on special register %tid.x, behind `xor.b32`){{$}}
